; NOTE: Generated by Inputs/gen-win64-unwind-tests.py. Do not edit by hand.

; Unwinding through tail calls that grow and shrink the stack argument area.
;
; Run under Windows. The harness (Inputs/win64-unwind-harness.c) runs each
; case to completion, then single-steps it: at each instruction of the
; function under test, and of the function it tail calls, the unwinder must
; recover the caller and its nonvolatile registers, and the system exception
; dispatcher must be able to unwind to a handler in the harness.
;
; Selectors go from the tail call that needs the most stack down to one with
; the same size as the caller's own arguments (growing cases), or from the
; largest shrink (shrinking cases); the last selector is a return. The csr
; cases keep values in callee-saved registers across a call, including the one
; stored over the caller's return address.

